The vendored source archive manpages-l10n.tar.xz is reconstructed from
the baseline Slint pkgtools package for the same version.

Why this exists:
The legacy pkgtools.SlackBuild expected manpages-l10n.tar.xz in the
package directory, but that archive was not present in the repository.
The baseline pkgtools package does contain the localized manpages, so
the archive can be regenerated from that package artifact.

What is included:
- Languages: de el es fa fr id it nb nl pl pt_BR pt_PT ru sv tr uk
- Pages: explodepkg installpkg makepkg pkgtool removepkg upgradepkg

What is intentionally not included:
- English manpages from manpages/
- pkgdiff.8 translations, because the baseline package does not ship
  localized pkgdiff manpages

How to regenerate:
1. Obtain the matching baseline package artifact, for example:
   /tmp/pkgtools-15.1-noarch-1slint.txz
2. From this directory run:
   ./make-manpages-l10n.sh /tmp/pkgtools-15.1-noarch-1slint.txz
3. Rebuild with:
   fakeroot slkbuild -X

The helper script verifies that every expected localized manpage exists
in the baseline package before rewriting manpages-l10n.tar.xz. It also
normalizes file order, timestamps, and ownership in the archive so the
result is deterministic for the same input package.
